# Local API-base override (see .env.local.example). The repo-root .gitignore has `.env` and
# `*.env`, and NEITHER matches `.env.local` — so without this line the file .env.local.example
# tells every developer to create lands in the next `git add -A`, on a public repo.
.env*.local
